  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Like animal and plant cells, the cells of microorganisms are also surrounded by a cell membrane. Cells of fungi additionally have a cell wall, but they do not have chloroplasts, so they cannot make their own food through photosynthesis. Bacteria do not have a well-defined nucleus and a nuclear membrane. Instead they have a nucleoid. This feature distinguishes them from cells of yeast, protozoa, algae, fungi, plants, and animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.211,
            0.883,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have only looked at a few basic cell structures here. The cell has other components about which you will learn in higher classes. For observing subcellular components, we need microscopes with high magnification. An electron microscope magnifies the cell about 10,00,000 times, where we can see more structures present in a cell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.321,
            0.883,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By now, you must have understood that all living beings, including microorganisms, are made up of one or more cells. Their cells differ in size, shape, and structure. Plant and animal cells also have some differences. Understanding these differences helps us learn how these organisms function differently."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.412,
            0.883,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this chapter, we have learnt about the beneficial microorganisms. However, there are some microbes that cause diseases in plants and animals including humans. We will learn about some of the diseases caused by microbes in the next chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.056,
            0.484,
            0.203,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.056,
                0.484,
                0.203,
                0.627
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.514,
            0.362,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.547,
            0.859,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Microorganisms are small-sized organisms and are not visible to the unaided eye."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.582,
            0.86,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "They can live in all kinds of environments, and even in the bodies of plants and animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.618,
            0.859,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "They are either unicellular or multicellular. Bacteria and protozoans are unicellular; fungi can be unicellular or multicellular, while plants and animals are multicellular."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.671,
            0.495,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The cell is a basic unit of life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.689,
            0.859,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The body of all living organisms is made up of cells. A cell contains various components which help the organisms perform their functions and survive."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.742,
            0.859,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A typical cell is bounded by a cell membrane, filled with cytoplasm and contains a nucleus. Plant, fungal, and bacterial cells have an extra covering, called a cell wall, around the cell membrane. Bacteria lack a well-defined nucleus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.811,
            0.858,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cells differ in shape and size. Their shape is related to the function performed by them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.847,
            0.843,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Bacteria, fungi, and protozoa are different kinds of microorganisms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.866,
            0.859,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Viruses are also small in size, but they are different from other microorganisms since they reproduce only inside the host organism."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
